<!--
  BlockML Core — primitive type branch

  FQN: org.blockml.core.PrimitiveType
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.core">

  <idea>Branch for scalar value types — single atomic values.</idea>

  <documentation>Abstract branch for built-in scalar ValueTypes. Numeric branch:
    org.blockml.type.Number (Integer, Float, Decimal). Other scalars: String, Boolean.

    Dual role (Java analogy — int vs Integer, only as illustration):
    • Property slot (type="Integer" or scalar property value) → inline scalar — no nested Block
      instance; the value is stored directly (LiteralValue).
    • Everywhere else (composition child, suggestion, constraint payload as Block instance, …)
      → Block instance of the primitive type (&lt;Integer value="5"/&gt;).

    Same FQN in both roles; validator and renderer choose semantics from usage context.</documentation>
  <name>PrimitiveType</name>
  <type>core:PrimitiveType</type>
  <baseType>core:ValueType</baseType>
  <abstract />

  <properties>
    <value type="_self">
      <documentation>The value of the primitive.</documentation>
    </value>
  </properties>
</block>